\subsubsection{Nested mixed model: Regions and villages}
\mbox{\cde{CM02: RLab-AppStat/v14-u31.R}}

<<CM02-1,eval=FALSE>>=
data("v-lmm-soils", package = "SelectionTools")
m.soils <- st.lmm(
    fixed = yield ~ region,
    random = ~region:village,
    data = soils,
    method = "moments"
)
m.soils
@

\begin{Soutput}
Linear mixed model fitted by the method of moments

Model:
  Data:      soils
  Fixed:     yield ~ region
  Random:    ~region:village

Design: balanced nested

ANOVA (method of moments, exact F):
  Source          DF1  DF2        SS        MS        F        p
  region            2    3  208.0000  104.0000   2.7857   0.2071
  region:village    3   18  112.0000   37.3333  12.9231  <0.0001
  Residual         18        52.0000    2.8889                  

Unconstrained moment variance estimates:
  Component       Estimate
  region:village    8.6111
  Residual          2.8889
\end{Soutput}

The \cde{region:village} row tests whether the variance among villages
within regions is zero. Its mean square is
compared with the residual mean square, giving an exact F-test with
3 and 18 degrees of freedom.

The shared printing options also show the expected mean squares and the
construction of the F-tests after the variance component estimates.

<<CM02-details,eval=FALSE>>=
st.options(list(
    print.ems = TRUE,
    print.test.construction = TRUE
))
m.soils
@

\begin{Soutput}
Linear mixed model fitted by the method of moments

Model:
  Data:      soils
  Fixed:     yield ~ region
  Random:    ~region:village

Design: balanced nested

ANOVA (method of moments, exact F):
  Source          DF1  DF2        SS        MS        F        p
  region            2    3  208.0000  104.0000   2.7857   0.2071
  region:village    3   18  112.0000   37.3333  12.9231  <0.0001
  Residual         18        52.0000    2.8889                  

Unconstrained moment variance estimates:
  Component       Estimate
  region:village    8.6111
  Residual          2.8889

Expected mean squares (EMS):
  Convention: Underwood (1997), Cornfield-Tukey; restricted interactions
  EMS(region)         = s2 + 4 s2(region:village) + 8 theta(region)
  EMS(region:village) = s2 + 4 s2(region:village)
  EMS(Residual)       = s2

Test construction:

  region (exact F-test)
    Numerator MS: region
    Denominator MS: region:village

  region:village (exact F-test)
    Numerator MS: region:village
    Denominator MS: Residual
\end{Soutput}


The least-squares means describe the mean yield in each region, with
uncertainty accounting for the random variation among villages within regions.

<<CM02-region-means,eval=FALSE>>=
st.lsm(m.soils, ~region)
@

\begin{Soutput}
Least-squares means (exact)
  region  lsmeans      SE  DF  lower.CL  upper.CL
  I        9.0000  2.1602   3    2.1251   15.8749
  II      14.0000  2.1602   3    7.1251   20.8749
  III      7.0000  2.1602   3    0.1251   13.8749
Confidence level: 0.9500
LSD=9.7225 HSD=12.7663 (alpha=0.05)
\end{Soutput}

The region effects are deviations from the equally weighted average of
the three region means. A positive effect indicates a region mean above
this average; a negative effect indicates a mean below it.
The tests compare these deviations with zero.

<<CM02-region-effects,eval=FALSE>>=
st.lsm(
    m.soils,
    ~region,
    method = "eff"
)
@

\begin{Soutput}
Least-squares mean contrasts (exact)
  contrast    estimate      SE  DF  lower.CL  upper.CL        t       p
  I effect     -1.0000  1.7638   3   -6.6133    4.6133  -0.5669  0.6104
  II effect     4.0000  1.7638   3   -1.6133    9.6133   2.2678  0.1081
  III effect   -3.0000  1.7638   3   -8.6133    2.6133  -1.7008  0.1875
p-value adjustment: none; confidence level: 0.9500
\end{Soutput}

A one-factor ANOVA compares the six villages as fixed levels.
The village factor has six levels, \cde{A}--\cde{F}, with two villages
in each region.
The residual variation describes differences among fields within villages.

