\subsubsection{Crossed and nested effects: Rapeseed}

The rapeseed trial compares plant height for 20 genotypes in two environments,
with three replicates in each environment. Genotypes occur in both environments,
whereas replicates are nested within environments.

<<CM15-1,eval=FALSE>>=
data("v-lmm-rapeseed", package = "SelectionTools")
st.options(list(
    print.ems = TRUE,
    print.test.construction = TRUE
))
@

Genotype, environment and their interaction are fixed effects. The random
\cde{rep:env} term describes variation among replicates within environments.
The method of moments estimates the replicate and residual variances and
provides F-tests for the model terms. The shared printing options include
the expected mean squares and the construction of these tests in the model
output.

<<CM15-2,eval=FALSE>>=
m.rape <- st.lmm(
    fixed = hgt ~ geno * env,
    random = ~rep:env,
    data = rapeseed,
    method = "moments"
)
m.rape
@

\begin{Soutput}
Linear mixed model fitted by the method of moments

Model:
  Data:      rapeseed
  Fixed:     hgt ~ geno * env
  Random:    ~rep:env

Design: general balanced orthogonal

ANOVA (method of moments, exact F):
  Source    DF1  DF2          SS         MS        F        p
  geno       19   76  11425.8667   601.3614   6.6832  <0.0001
  env         1    4   9469.6333  9469.6333  51.5051   0.0020
  geno:env   19   76   1204.3667    63.3877   0.7045   0.8031
  env:rep     4   76    735.4333   183.8583   2.0433   0.0967
  Residual   76        6838.5667    89.9811                  

Unconstrained moment variance estimates:
  Component  Estimate
  env:rep      4.6939
  Residual    89.9811

Expected mean squares (EMS):
  Convention: Underwood (1997), Cornfield-Tukey; restricted interactions
  EMS(geno)     = 1 s2                  + 6 theta(geno)
  EMS(env)      = 1 s2 + 20 s2(env:rep) + 60 theta(env)
  EMS(geno:env) = 1 s2                  + 3 theta(geno:env)
  EMS(env:rep)  = 1 s2 + 20 s2(env:rep)
  EMS(Residual) = 1 s2

Test construction:

  geno (exact F-test)
    Numerator MS: geno
    Denominator MS: Residual

  env (exact F-test)
    Numerator MS: env
    Denominator MS: env:rep

  geno:env (exact F-test)
    Numerator MS: geno:env
    Denominator MS: Residual

  env:rep (exact F-test)
    Numerator MS: env:rep
    Denominator MS: Residual
\end{Soutput}

The environment test uses the replicate-within-environment mean square as
its denominator, with four denominator degrees of freedom. Genotype and
genotype-by-environment interaction are tested against the residual mean
square, with 76 denominator degrees of freedom. Genotype and environment
have significant effects; the interaction is not significant.

The genotype least-squares means describe plant height averaged over both environments.

