  Sum          57        58        57        60        59 291
\end{Soutput}

The model includes fixed environment effects and fixed replicate effects
within environments, separately for each trait. The random genotype and
genotype-by-environment effects each have a full covariance matrix across
the seven traits. A separate full residual covariance matrix is estimated
for each environment. The genotype covariance matrix describes the
relationships among genotype effects shared across environments.

<<M47-1,eval=FALSE>>=
m.met.seven <- st.lmm(
    fixed = cbind(YLD, HLW, TKW, PLH, DH, DM, SC) ~ env + rep:env,
    random = ~gen + gen:env,
    cov = ~at(env):units,
    data = barley.seven.traits,
    random.test = "none",
    control = list(backend = "block")
)
st.lmm.components(m.met.seven, "covariance", block = "gen")
@

\begin{Soutput}
           YLD     HLW      TKW       PLH        DH       DM       SC
  YLD  60.3784  2.8817  24.9291  143.3567  -50.6606 -34.4759  -4.3092
  HLW   2.8817  2.5724   2.7317   17.6852   -4.2309  -2.7620  -0.3568
  TKW  24.9291  2.7317  17.3686   68.3571  -21.1640 -14.0188  -2.1689
  PLH 143.3567 17.6852  68.3571  433.0834 -120.8631 -83.6531 -11.2377
  DH  -50.6606 -4.2309 -21.1640 -120.8631   69.2974  48.1663   1.9682
  DM  -34.4759 -2.7620 -14.0188  -83.6531   48.1663  36.0201   1.2429
  SC   -4.3092 -0.3568  -2.1689  -11.2377    1.9682   1.2429   0.6694
\end{Soutput}

The fitted genotype covariance is positive definite. The genotype-by-
environment covariance has rank six, with a numerically zero eigenvalue.

The genetic correlation matrix expresses the same relationships on a
common scale.

