\subsubsection{Multiple regression: Partial tests and term order}
The default Type III tests assess each predictor conditional on the other.
Reversing the predictor order preserves these tests and the fitted model.
\mbox{\cde{CM12: RLab-BioStat/v19-u21.R}}

<<CM12-1,eval=FALSE>>=
data("v-lmm-rats", package = "SelectionTools")
m.rats <- st.lmm(
    y ~ x.1 + x.2,
    data = rats,
    method = "moments"
)
m.rats
@

\begin{Soutput}
Linear model fitted by the method of moments

Model:
  Data:      rats
  Fixed:     y ~ x.1 + x.2

ANOVA (method of moments, exact F):
