   9  9        2.1548
  10  10       2.0612
\end{Soutput}

\subsection{Genomic prediction with a multi-environment trial}

\subsubsection{Joint analysis of plot data}

The multi-environment plot table and its marker calls are loaded for this
example. \cde{st.load.vcf.data} stores the marker data under
\cde{"maize.lattice"}.

<<tropmaize-lattice-mask,eval=FALSE>>=
data("v-lmm-tropmaize-lattice", package = "SelectionTools")
data("v-tropmaize-vcf", package = "SelectionTools")
st.load.vcf.data(v.tropmaize.vcf, data.set = "maize.lattice")
@

\begin{Soutput}
M (data set 'maize.lattice'): New data set generated 'maize.lattice'
M (data set 'maize.lattice'): No. of individuals: 264, no. of markers: 1076
\end{Soutput}

The relationship matrix is extracted from that marker data set. The
first ten genotype levels identify the entries whose responses will be
hidden in every environment.

<<tropmaize-lattice-matrix,eval=FALSE>>=
maize.lattice.A <- st.get.A("maize.lattice")
maize.lattice.missing.gen <- levels(tropmaize.lattice$gen)[seq_len(10)]
@

The copy \cde{maize.lattice.masked} retains every plot row. Responses
for the selected genotypes are replaced by \cde{NA}, including their
records in different environments.

<<tropmaize-lattice-mask-b,eval=FALSE>>=
maize.lattice.masked <- tropmaize.lattice
maize.lattice.masked$y[
    maize.lattice.masked$gen %in% maize.lattice.missing.gen
] <- NA_real_
@

The fixed formula gives each environment its own mean. The random
formula includes genotype, replicate within environment, block within
replicate and environment, and genotype-by-environment terms.
\cde{ucov} supplies the matrix for \cde{gen}; \cde{data} selects the
masked plot table.

<<tropmaize-lattice-one-step-fit,eval=FALSE>>=
maize.lattice.one.step <- st.lmm(
    fixed = y ~ env,
    random = ~gen + env:rep + env:rep:block + gen:env,
    ucov = list(gen = maize.lattice.A),
    data = maize.lattice.masked
)
maize.lattice.one.step
@

\begin{Soutput}
Linear mixed model fitted by REML

Model:
  Data:      maize.lattice.masked
  Fixed:     y ~ env
  Random:    ~gen + env:rep + env:rep:block + gen:env
  Residual:  ~units
  Covariance: gen (264 levels; supplied matrix)

Convergence:
  converged: projected score tolerance met

Fixed effects (Satterthwaite):
  Term  DF1    DF2        F        p
  env     4  19.26  61.9321  <0.0001

Random effects (likelihood-ratio tests):
  Term           DF         LR        p
  gen             1  2950.7508  <0.0001
